    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Workday is a publicly traded enterprise software company, founded in 2005 and headquartered in Pleasanton, CA, that offers cloud-based applications for HR, finance, and IT. The company trades on the ticker WDAY and reported revenue of $9,552,000,000 for the fiscal year ending January 31, 2026, according to its most recent 10-K filing.\n\nThe company describes its platform as an enterprise AI system centered on HR, finance, and IT operations. Its tracked AI product, Workday AI, encompasses skills-based talent management, predictive analytics, and sensitive HR data handling. The company's website also promotes a product or integration called Sana alongside what it terms agentic AI, describing agents capable of finding, building, acting, and automating processes across those three business domains.\n\nWorkday is named in nine federal civil cases across multiple district courts, including multiple actions styled Meckfessel Poletti v. Workday, Inc. in the Eastern District of California, Williams v. Workday, Inc. in the Northern District of Georgia, Elias v. Workday, Inc. in the Northern District of California, Hill v. Workday, Inc. in both the District of Maryland and the Eastern District of Virginia, and additional cases in the Districts of Colorado and Maryland. The range of courts and plaintiffs suggests ongoing litigation exposure across several jurisdictions.",
